; GLQuakeNull -- milestone 2: GLQuake's timedemos against the RadeonGL
; minigl.library with the null card (docs/core.md, lib/nullcard.c). The
; real core, emitter and ring writer run; every packet the GPU would read
; goes through the packet checker. Each demo runs in the background
; (DEV:Test/RunNull) with up to 10 minutes; one that does not finish is
; reported with Status and a screen grab, and the script moves on.
; Per demo: DEV:Test/null-<demo>.log = GLQuake's text + the library's
; summary (frames, dwords, draws, checker errors, unimplemented slots).
; Needs: gmake glquake glquake-data rgl-lib.
; LIMIT 2100
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Stack 1000000
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/null-#?
Echo "=== demo1 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNull demo1
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/null-demo1.done
Type DEV:Test/null-demo1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/null-demo1-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== demo2 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNull demo2
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/null-demo2.done
Type DEV:Test/null-demo2.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/null-demo2-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== demo3 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNull demo3
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/null-demo3.done
Type DEV:Test/null-demo3.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/null-demo3-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
